/* book: lead: A TRIAC conducts in both directions, so one TRIAC replaces the antiparallel SCR pair of an AC voltage controller and needs only one gate circuit. Delaying its turn-on in each half cycle cuts away the start of every half wave, and the RMS voltage at the load falls smoothly. Lamp dimmers and fan regulators use it. The exam asks how the gate is fired with positive and negative pulses, and how the RC- */
/* book Figure 5.2.1: The dimmer of the worked examples. The capacitor voltage lags the supply by 72.3° and reaches the 30 V DIAC breakover at 90°, so the TRIAC fires at α = 90° in both half cycles. */
